          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter 9 — The Amazing World of Solutes, Solvents, and Solutions",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.888,
            0.029,
            0.923,
            0.045
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "149"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.102,
            0.263,
            0.124
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Snapshots"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.14,
            0.823,
            0.175
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A solution is said to be formed when two or more substances mix to form a uniform mixture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.179,
            0.824,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the solution formed by dissolving a solid in a liquid, the solid component is known as a solute and the liquid component is known as a solvent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.825,
            0.058,
            0.96,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.825,
                0.058,
                0.96,
                0.22
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.218,
            0.825,
            0.254
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In a solution formed by mixing two liquids, the component present in less quantity is known as solute and the other component is called solvent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.258,
            0.824,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A solution in which the maximum amount of solute has been dissolved, and no more of it can be dissolved at that temperature is called a saturated solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.314,
            0.824,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A solution in which more solute can be dissolved at a given temperature is called an unsaturated solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.353,
            0.824,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solubility is the maximum amount of solute that can be dissolved in a fixed quantity (100 mL) of a solution or a solvent at a particular temperature."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.393,
            0.824,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Generally, in liquids, the solubility of solids increases and that of gases decreases with an increase in temperature."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.432,
            0.749,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The amount of matter present in an object is known as its mass."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.455,
            0.813,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The space occupied by an object or a substance is known as its volume."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.478,
            0.824,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Devices used to measure mass and volume are a weighing balance and a measuring cylinder, respectively."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.516,
            0.823,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The mass per unit volume of a substance is known as its density (Density = Mass/Volume)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.556,
            0.824,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Generally, density decreases with an increase in temperature and pressure affects density differently depending on the state of matter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.631,
            0.392,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Keep the curiosity alive"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.672,
            0.743,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. State whether the statements given below are True [T] or False [F]. Correct the false statement(s)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.712,
            0.743,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Oxygen gas is more soluble in hot water rather than in cold water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.749,
            0.607,
            0.767
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) A mixture of sand and water is a solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.767,
            0.743,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) The amount of space occupied by any object is called its mass."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.804,
            0.743,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) An unsaturated solution has more solute dissolved than a saturated solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.841,
            0.743,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(v) The presence of different gases in the atmosphere is also a uniform mixture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
